    "title": "Didn't file your taxes in time? Tennessee given new June deadline",
    "text": "LOCALWhen are taxes due? Why all of Tennessee was granted an extension Jordan GreenMemphis Commercial AppealApril 13, 2026Updated April 16, 2026, 9:50 a.m. CTThis story has been updated with new information from the IRS.Tax Day has come and gone in Tennessee, but if you missed the deadline, it's not the end of the world.On April 3, the IRS announced that counties severely impacted by the winter storm from January would get an extra month to file their taxes. Then, on April 15, a few hours before the deadline, the IRS announced it would expand the tax deadline for all 95 counties in the state.Already a subscriber? Sign inTwo ways to continue readingPay Annually$149SAVE 50% versus MonthlySubscribeSubscribers getBEST DEALFull access to commercialappeal.com including articles, videos, and moreA subscription to shareAccess to the eNewspaperShow featuresMonthly$1for the first monthSubscribeSubscribers getFull access to commercialappeal.com including articles, videos, and moreA subscription to shareAccess to the eNewspaperShow featuresInterested in other subscriptions? Learn more",
